// sentinel-dedup.kql — logical deduplication view for KEEL SIEM events in
// Microsoft Sentinel / Azure Monitor (roadmap task-80).
//
// Why this view exists: KEEL delivery is AT-LEAST-ONCE
// (engine/telemetry/outbox.mjs RECEIVER_DEDUP_CONTRACT). The same event can be
// physically ingested more than once — retry after an uncertain acknowledgement,
// crash after remote acceptance before the checkpoint commit, or an
// operator-requested replay — always under the SAME KEEL event id.
// x-ms-client-request-id is diagnostic only and is NOT a dedup key.
//
// Dedup key: (TenantRef, DestinationId, KeelEventId) — the receiver dedup
// contract fields. This view collapses physical duplicates to one logical event,
// keeping the row with the latest TimeGenerated (identical events differ, if at
// all, only in ingestion lag). Always query KeelEventsLogical (or run this
// query), never the raw KeelEvents_CL table, when counting or alerting.

let KeelEventsLogical =
    KeelEvents_CL
    | summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, *) by TenantRef, DestinationId, KeelEventId;
KeelEventsLogical
